{%- doc -%}
  The three header actions, written out as rows for the drawer.

  On a phone the header keeps its icons but loses the room to explain them, and
  the drawer is where a menu is read rather than glanced at — so search, account
  and wishlist appear here as labelled rows under the navigation instead of as
  three more glyphs in a crowded row.

  The search row is the same control the header uses, not a link to a search
  page: it opens `#search-modal`, so the drawer and the header reach the same
  dialog and there is one search on the site rather than two.

  A row is dropped rather than disabled when it has nowhere to go — customer
  accounts switched off, or no wishlist page chosen — because a drawer is a list
  of places you can get to, and a dead row in it is a worse answer than a
  shorter list. The header keeps its silent wishlist placeholder for spacing
  reasons that do not apply here.

  @param {string} [wishlist_url] - The wishlist page. No URL, no row.
  @param {string} [class] - Additional CSS classes.

  @example
  {% render 'ui-drawer-actions', wishlist_url: section.settings.wishlist_url %}
{%- enddoc -%}

<ul class="ui-drawer-actions list-unstyled {{ class }}">
  <li>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="ui-drawer-actions__item"
      on:click="#search-modal/showDialog"
    >
      <span class="ui-drawer-actions__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        {{- 'icon-ui-search.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </span>
      {{ 'content.search' | t }}
    </button>
  </li>

  {%- if shop.customer_accounts_enabled -%}
    <li>
      <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}" class="ui-drawer-actions__item">
        <span class="ui-drawer-actions__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- 'icon-ui-account.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </span>
        {{ 'content.account_title' | t }}
      </a>
    </li>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if wishlist_url != blank -%}
    <li>
      <a href="{{ wishlist_url }}" class="ui-drawer-actions__item">
        <span class="ui-drawer-actions__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- 'icon-ui-wishlist.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </span>
        {{ 'accessibility.wishlist' | t }}
      </a>
    </li>
  {%- endif -%}
</ul>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
   * A hairline rather than a gap, because the navigation above this can be
   * anything from three rows to a dozen: a gap large enough to read as a break
   * under three items is lost under twelve, and one that survives twelve leaves
   * a hole under three.
   */
  .ui-drawer-actions {
    margin-block-start: 16px;
    padding-block-start: 8px;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--ui-color-border-gray);
  }

  .ui-drawer-actions__item {
    display: flex;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    font-family: var(--ui-font-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: var(--ui-font-body-weight);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-foreground-heading);
    text-align: start;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* The kit's glyphs are all drawn at a viewBox of 20 with a 1.5 stroke, so a
     20px box renders them at the weight the header draws them. Sizing the
     wrapper alone would leave the svg at its intrinsic size inside it. */
  .ui-drawer-actions__icon,
  .ui-drawer-actions__icon > svg {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    color: currentcolor;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
